# The tools ship unstripped, deliberately.
#
# Release builds are RelWithDebInfo and the debug information is left in place
# rather than stripped or split into a -dbgsym package. dsdlc is a compiler for
# an avionics-adjacent wire format: when it misbehaves in the field, the symbols
# needed to read a backtrace or a core file have to already be on the machine
# that produced it. A -dbgsym package puts them one apt-install away, which is
# one apt-install too many when the failure is not reproducible.
#
# The cost is package size and this override. Revisit if the packages grow
# enough for that to matter.
#
# Deliberately no file hint: lintian releases disagree on how the hint is
# rendered (bracketed on 24.04, bare on 22.04), and a hint that does not match
# the running version is silently inert -- it reports mismatched-override and
# lets the original tag through. Matching on the tag alone works on both.
llvm-dsdl: unstripped-binary-or-object
